The Mercedes-Benz C-Class with the AMG Line package is a popular configuration that adds sporty aesthetics and some performance-oriented features to the standard C-Class sedan (W206 generation). It sits below the full-fledged AMG performance models (C43, C63).

Here's an evaluation based on the provided data and scoring guide:

*   **price\_usd**: The price for a C300 AMG Line is around $48,550 USD (Source [4]) or £54,150 OTR in the UK (Source [28]), which is significantly above the $35,000 market average. Score: -0.30.
*   **total\_cost\_estimate\_5yr\_usd**: Mercedes-Benz vehicles, even non-AMG performance models, tend to have higher ownership costs than average due to depreciation, maintenance, and insurance. Score: -0.20.
*   **insurance\_usd\_yr**: Mercedes-Benz C-Class models are in higher insurance groups than average cars. Score: -0.20.
*   **maint\_usd\_yr**: Maintenance costs for Mercedes-Benz are generally higher than average (Source [38] mentions higher service costs for W206 compared to W205). Score: -0.50.
*   **repair\_risk\_score**: Mercedes-Benz has an average to slightly above-average reliability reputation, but not in the top tier like Lexus or Toyota. Score: 0.00.
*   **hp**: The C300 AMG Line typically has 255 hp (Source [4, 7, 8, 12, 14, 20, 26, 27, 35]). This is above the 200 hp average. Score: 0.30.
*   **torque**: The C300 AMG Line has 295 lb-ft (400 Nm) (Source [8, 14, 20, 26, 27, 35]). This is well above the 190 lb-ft average. Score: 0.50.
*   **cylinder\_count**: 4 cylinders (Source [8, 14, 20, 26, 27, 28, 35]). This is common, so average. Score: 0.00.
*   **engine\_displacement**: 2.0L (1999 cc or 1992 cc) (Source [14, 20, 26, 27, 28, 35]). This is around the average for a 4-cylinder engine in this segment. Score: 0.00.
*   **accel\_0\_60\_sec**: Around 5.3-6.0 seconds (Source [7, 8, 12, 14, 27, 35]). This is significantly faster than the 7.5-second average. Score: 0.70.
*   **top\_speed**: 155 mph (250 km/h) (Source [12, 14, 27]). This is around the average for a non-performance luxury sedan. Score: 0.00.
*   **drive\_type**: RWD is standard, AWD (4Matic) is optional (Source [7, 8, 14, 16, 20, 27, 35]). RWD scores +1.00 according to the guide. Score: 1.00.
*   **transmission\_type**: 9-speed automatic (9G-TRONIC) (Source [1, 3, 7, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16, 27, 28, 35]). This is a modern, smooth automatic. Score: 1.00.
*   **offroad\_ability**: Low ground clearance, RWD/AWD sedan, not designed for off-road. Score: 1.00 (based on guide examples).
*   **braking\_dist\_ft**: Not explicitly stated, but expected to be good for the segment. Score: 0.00.
*   **size**: Length is around 4751-4793 mm (Source [2, 3, 6, 9, 13, 14, 15, 19, 20, 24, 25, 27, 29, 31, 34, 36]). This is slightly larger than the 4600mm average. Score: 0.10.
*   **wheelbase**: 2865 mm (112.8 inches) (Source [2, 6, 7, 9, 13, 15, 17, 18, 19, 20, 24, 27, 33, 34, 36]). This is longer than the 2700mm average. Score: 0.20.
*   **body\_style**: 4-door Sedan (Source [6, 7, 27, 34]). Score: 0.00.
*   **seats**: 5 seats (Source [7, 27, 34]). Score: 0.00.
*   **cargo\_space**: 455 liters (around 16 cu ft) (Source [2, 9, 13, 14, 17, 20, 25, 27, 29, 31, 34, 41]). This is around the 15 cu ft average. Score: 0.00.
*   **rear\_space**: Improved over the previous generation, but still not class-leading compared to larger sedans (Source [2, 3, 7, 18, 30, 38, 41]). Score: 0.00.
*   **ground\_clearance\_in**: Around 9.7 cm (3.8 inches) to 164mm (6.4 inches) (Source [13, 20, 25, 29, 31, 33, 34]). AMG Line often has a lower sport suspension (Source [4, 35]), bringing it closer to the lower end. Score: -0.20.
*   **turn\_radius\_ft**: 10.64 meters (34.9 ft) with optional rear-axle steering, otherwise likely slightly larger (Source [9, 17, 20, 24]). This is slightly better than the 36 ft average with the option. Score: 0.10.
*   **mpg**: EPA estimates around 25-29 mpg combined (Source [7, 35]). Real-world can vary (Source [7, 35, 38, 39]). This is around the 30 mpg average. Score: 0.00.
*   **co2\_g\_km**: Around 150-153 g/km for petrol models (Source [12, 27]). This is below the 175 g/km average. Score: 0.30.
*   **electric\_range\_mi**: Not a full EV or PHEV (mild hybrid only). Score: -1.00.
*   **charge\_speed\_kw**: Not applicable (mild hybrid only). Score: -1.00.
*   **style\_sleek\_vs\_boxy**: Modern sedan design, leaning towards sleek. Score: 0.40.
